    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "Malignant phyllodes tumour with heterologous rhabdomyoblastic differentiation",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Malignant phyllodes tumour with heterologous rhabdomyoblastic differentiation\nMalignant phyllodes tumour shows marked stromal cellularity, moderate to marked stromal atypia with bizarre tumour giant cells, stromal overgrowth and brisk mitotic activity of 33 per 10 high power fields (field diameter 0.66mm), focally permeative borders. Occasional polygonal strap-like cells with eccentric nuclei and ample pink cytoplasm are observed among the abnormal spindle cell population, with myogenin and desmin immunohistochemical expression supporting rhabdomyoblastic differentiation.",
    "source": "Puay H. Tan",
    "copyright": "",
